Set up the development environment – Install and configure the required software, tools, frameworks, and databases.

Develop the system – Write the code and build the required features and modules.

Implement the database – Create tables, relationships, queries, and data-management functions.

Integrate modules – Connect different components so that they work together as one system.

Implement security – Add authentication, authorization, data protection, and other security measures.

Perform continuous testing – Test individual features during development and fix errors as they are found.

Review progress – Compare development progress with the project plan and requirements.

Make improvements – Modify features or implementation based on testing and feedback.
